1. THE LAW: A ∪ (A ∩ B) = A, A ∩ (A ∪ B) = A
   checked on all 256 choices of 2 subset(s) of U = {1, 2, 3, 4}: True

2. ONE INSTANCE, WORKED
   A = {1, 2}, B = {2, 3}, C = {3, 4}, A' = {3, 4}, B' = {1, 4}
   A ∪ (A ∩ B) = A ∪ {2} = {1, 2} = A
   A ∩ (A ∪ B) = A ∩ {1, 2, 3} = {1, 2} = A

3. THE SAME LAW IN LOGIC: p ∨ (p ∧ q) = p, p ∧ (p ∨ q) = p
   every row of the truth table agrees, which is why the member-by-member check is a proof:
   p  q   left  right
   T  T   T     T
   T  F   T     T
   F  T   F     F
   F  F   F     F
